  "hallmark": "the six black stripes running head to tail, and the scutellum that reaches almost to the abdomen's tip",
  "reference": {
    "title": "Betrachtungen über die Farbenpracht der Insekten, plate I figure 3",
    "artist": "Karl Brunner von Wattenwyl",
    "year": 1897,
    "source": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Betrachtungen_uber_die_Farbenpracht_der_Insekten_(Plate_I)_(9237127969).jpg",
    "licence": "Public domain (PD-old-70-expired)"
  },
  "doc": [
    "*Graphosoma italicum*, dorsal — the Italian striped shield bug.",
    "",
    "Traced from figure 3 of plate I of Brunner von Wattenwyl's *Betrachtungen",
    "über die Farbenpracht der Insekten* (1897), where it is captioned under the",
    "name *Graphosoma lineatum* — the two have since been separated, and the",
    "animal figured, with the whole pronotum striped rather than spotted at the",
    "front, is *italicum*. `references/graphosoma-italicum.jpg` is the sheet and",
    "the bug is figure 3, low and left of centre.",
    "",
    "It is a *small* figure on a large plate — Brunner's sheet is about colour in",
    "insects generally, so it carries a locust, four scarabs and three",
    "butterflies as well, and this bug gets fifty pixels. The same thing was true",
    "of the seven-spot and the answer is the same: what a shield bug needs from a",
    "reference is the outline, the scutellum and where the stripes run, and all",
    "three survive at that size. The proportions were then checked against the",
    "published measurements — 8 to 12 mm long and about 0.72 as wide as long.",
    "",
    "## What the drawing has to get right",
    "",
    "The **stripes**, which are what `markings: 'stripes'` means on this record",
    "and the reason this animal is in the collection at all: six black lines",
    "running head to tail, straight across the pronotum and converging down the",
    "scutellum. Drawn as capsules clipped to the surface they are on, three a",
    "side, mirrored — because a plate that placed them separately on each side",
    "would be drawing one specimen's asymmetry rather than the species.",
    "",
    "Then the **scutellum**. On a green shield bug it is a triangle between the",
    "wings; on this one it reaches almost to the tip of the abdomen and the",
    "hemelytra are reduced to a narrow strip either side of it. That is the",
    "character that separates the two at a glance and it is why the corium here is",
    "authored as a long thin shape rather than as half a wing.",
    "",
    "Then the **connexivum** — the rim of the abdomen showing outside the wings,",
    "banded black and red. Six short strokes marching down it, clipped to the",
    "abdomen.",
    "",
    "## Plate space",
    "",
    "y = 0 at the front of the head, y = 1000 at the tip of the abdomen. The",
    "pronotum is 130 to 360 and the scutellum 350 to 900. Half-width 358, which",
    "is the 0.72 the measurements give."
  ],
